{
  "id": "endophenotype",
  "term": "endophenotype",
  "definition": "An endophenotype is a measurable neurobiological, physiological, cognitive, or social-cognitive marker that serves as an intermediate link between a disorder’s underlying polygenic basis and its clinical symptoms. In psychology and psychiatry research, it refers to a marker expected to be heritable, relatively independent of current illness state, and to run within families alongside the disorder.",
